paper/sections/3_method.tex:15:Sections~\ref{ssec:tools}--\ref{ssec:algorithm} describe our full
paper/sections/3_method.tex:17:\emph{headline number} in Table~\ref{tab:main_results} is produced by
paper/sections/3_method.tex:19:with Direct VLM, described in \S\ref{ssec:v6}. Section~\ref{ssec:refutation}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:28:    \label{fig:architecture}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:32:\label{ssec:tools}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:33:Each tool has a small, auditable contract; all tools are zero-VLM-call. The \texttt{domain\_descriptor} returns the task-anchored anomaly specification for the current domain (resolving generic-prior/task conflicts, e.g.\ D08 ``planned urbanisation IS the anomaly''). The \texttt{reference\_retriever} ranks the reference pool by DINOv2-CLS cosine similarity and returns the top-$k$. The \texttt{hotspot\_cropper} reads top-$k$ patch coordinates from an expert and crops the anomaly hotspot (used by the \emph{interpret} strategy). The \texttt{component\_counter} runs connected-component analysis on the expert hotspot map (logical anomalies). The \texttt{knowledge\_lookup} retrieves a domain keyword list for the VLM prompt (e.g.\ \emph{lesion, haemorrhage} for medical). Full tool signatures, I/O contracts, and implementations are in Appendix~\ref{app:tools}.
paper/sections/3_method.tex:36:\label{ssec:experts}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:45:\label{ssec:strategies}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:48:    \item[\textbf{fusion(expert)}.] One VLM call (direct), then post-hoc blend with the chosen expert's score: $s = (1-w)\,s_{\mathrm{v0}} + w\,\sigma\!\big((s_{\mathrm{exp}}-m)/m\big)$, with $w$ frozen on calibration ($w{=}0.2$ as the global default; per-domain $w$ in Appendix~\ref{app:per_domain_w}). Both \emph{fusion(SubspaceAD)} and \emph{fusion(AnomalyVFM)} are first-class strategies.
paper/sections/3_method.tex:51:    \item[\textbf{debate}.] Two VLM calls (proposer + advocate); rule-based aggregation (Appendix~\ref{app:debate}). Used when calibration shows VLM confidence is poorly calibrated on a domain.
paper/sections/3_method.tex:55:\label{ssec:router}
paper/sections/3_method.tex:58:The plan is computed once per (backbone, domain) pair and frozen before any test query. At inference time the agent looks up $\pi(d)$ and executes the strategy; no per-image router call is made. The final cost is the strategy's cost for that domain (Table~\ref{tab:main_results} reports an average of $0.92$ VLM calls/image on Qwen3.5).
