review-stage/codex_v9_review_r1_raw.out:2563:     8	We evaluate on \textbf{CrossDomainVAD-11}, spanning twelve domain codes grouped into 11 reported families: D1 MVTec-AD industrial, D2 GoodsAD retail, D3 SDNET2018 concrete infrastructure (dev only), D4 DermaMNIST dermoscopy, D5 BraTS2021 brain MRI, D5b BMAD brain MRI, D5c BMAD liver CT, D5d HyperKvasir GI endoscopy variant, D6 LEVIR-CD+ remote-sensing change, D7 HyperKvasir GI endoscopy, D8 RA21+BDD road, D9 MVTec-LOCO logical, D10 VisA industrial. Each domain contributes 20 calibration / 40 dev / 120 test items (D8: 98 test). All items are reference-based, paired with 1--10 normal references. Total test items $n{=}1418$ (fusion strategies drop D8 items lacking SubspaceAD support to $n{=}1298$ and fall back to direct on the rest). The full per-domain specification is in Appendix~\ref{app:benchmark}.
