review-stage/codex_v9_review_r2_raw.out:1478:./benchmark/results/active_learning/al_qwen35_D1_passive.json:1:[{"item_id": "D1_0085", "score": 0.15, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image displays a uniform brown leather-like texture that is consistent with the patterns and color variations seen in all four reference images. No distinct defects, scratches, or anomalies are observed.", "n_turns": 1, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0051", "score": 0.05, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The only potential anomaly (a small white speck) was refuted by observing similar features in the reference images, confirming it is a normal texture variation.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0043", "score": 0.08, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image displays a wood texture consistent with the reference images. No anomalous features were found after refuting the initial candidate, as the observed variations are natural to the material.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0063", "score": 0.08, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirmed that the surface features in the query image are consistent with the natural variations observed in the reference images, leading to a conclusion of no anomaly.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0058", "score": 0.15, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image displays a consistent wood grain texture and color that aligns well with the provided reference images. No obvious defects, scratches, or significant deviations from the normal patterns were observed.", "n_turns": 1, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0040", "score": 0.05, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image exhibits yellow and white bristles. The reference profiler confirms that 'bristle color variation' is an allowed variation and explicitly lists yellow as an expected color. Therefore, the observed difference is normal, not an anomaly.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0077", "score": 0.92, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image contains the 'actavis' logo on the black half of the capsule, which is absent in all provided reference images. This discrepancy confirms the image is anomalous.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0037", "score": 0.08, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirms that the query image's zipper and fabric features are consistent with the normal reference images, showing no unique defects or anomalies.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0039", "score": 0.05, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image displays a toothbrush with yellow and white bristles. The reference profiler explicitly states that 'bristle color variation' is an allowed variation and lists yellow as an expected color. Since the observed feature is within the normal range and no structural defects are visible, the image is classified as normal.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0081", "score": 0.15, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The query image shows a bottle rim that is visually consistent with the reference images. No obvious defects such as cracks, chips, or foreign objects are observed. The lighting and texture variations appear normal.", "n_turns": 1, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0011", "score": 0.08, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirms that the texture and speckle pattern in the query image are consistent with the normal reference images, with no unique anomalies detected.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0036", "score": 0.05, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The side-by-side comparison confirms that the features in the query image, specifically the component leg and soldering, are consistent with the normal variations observed in the reference images. No anomalies were detected.", "n_turns": 2, "error": null}, {"item_id": "D1_0014", "score": 0.05, "label_gt": 0, "domain_code": "D1", "rationale": "The only potential anomaly (a small white speck) was refuted by the side-by-side comparison, which showed similar f on Qwen3.5 it matches fusion. The oracle leaves 1.3--1.9 pp further headroom, suggesting a VLM-driven router reading image-level features may close more of the gap. Routing is calibrated from 20 items per domain; we evaluate a single expert backbone (DINOv2-giant) and a single frontier non-English VLM (SeedVL); the Route-C component-enumeration prototype (Appendix~\ref{app:routec}) remains at 60\% calibration accuracy on D9 and is not in the reported variant. The failed-variant ablation is GPT-5.4 calibration only. The online expert-signal override threshold ($\rho > 0.8$) is currently calibrated against patch-$k$-NN's normalised score; on industrial domains where SubspaceAD's raw distance is large, the override fires on essentially every \emph{normal}-predicted item and effectively reduces the strategy choice to ``fusion or interpret'' on those domains; a backbone-aware $\rho$ rescaling is left to future work.
review-stage/codex_v9_review_r3_raw.out:2997:review-stage/codex_review_r1_raw.out:2629:   152	The calibration router only beats fusion significantly on SeedVL; on GPT-5.4 it trails fusion by 0.5 pp (not significant) and on Qwen3.5 it matches fusion. The oracle leaves 1.3--1.9 pp further headroom, suggesting a VLM-driven router reading image-level features may close more of the gap. Routing is calibrated from 20 items per domain; we evaluate a single expert backbone (DINOv2-giant) and a single frontier non-English VLM (SeedVL); the Route-C component-enumeration prototype (Appendix~\ref{app:routec}) remains at 60\% calibration accuracy on D9 and is not in the reported variant. The failed-variant ablation is GPT-5.4 calibration only. The online expert-signal override threshold ($\rho > 0.8$) is currently calibrated against patch-$k$-NN's normalised score; on industrial domains where SubspaceAD's raw distance is large, the override fires on essentially every \emph{normal}-predicted item and effectively reduces the strategy choice to ``fusion or interpret'' on those domains; a backbone-aware $\rho$ rescaling is left to future work.
