benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5c.json:2092:            "positive_evidence": "The query object consists of one broad basal mass with two attached superior lobes/protrusions rising side-by-side and separated by a central gap. Across the references, the object appears as a single compact fragment (Refs 1 and 3), a main body with one detached small superior piece (Ref 2), or a vertically stacked/overlapping two-part form rather than two bilateral top projections from the same base (Ref 4). This is a strong arrangement/count mismatch.",
benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5c.json:2108:            "positive_evidence": "The whole-object silhouette in the query is broad, squat, and rounded at the bottom with two upper peaks, unlike the reference set, which shows either smaller single fragments, a crescent-like fragment, or a more vertical/stacked morphology. The global layout therefore departs from the reference regime.",
benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5c.json:2353:            "description": "Query shows a prominent additional lobulated protruding component attached at the upper-right of the main body, giving a two-piece/stacked appearance not seen in the references.",
benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5c.json:2386:            "positive_evidence": "The query object has a clear additional attached lobulated mass on the upper-right, creating a stacked/two-part silhouette with a disrupted junction. Across the references, the object is consistently a single main crescent/bean-like mass; even when projections exist, they are smaller contour extensions rather than a large separate-looking attached component. This difference is large, concrete, and visually obvious.",
benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj_k4_test_D5c.json:2618:            "description": "Query object has a tall upward-projecting appendage on the right side, creating a two-lobed/stacked silhouette not seen in the references.",
