benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D9.json:1081:        "evidence": "Two matching connector blocks are present on the left and right, each with the expected stacked orange levers, and they are connected by a central wire in the same overall arrangement as the normal references. No slot appears missing, no extra component is attached, and no physical breakage is visible.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D9.json:1523:        "reasoning": "1. The reference images show two normal assembly variants: a 2-connector version with a yellow wire (refs 1 and 2) and a 5-connector version with a red wire (ref 3). 2. The query image matches the 5-connector normal variant: both left and right sides have the same number of orange connector blocks, aligned in the expected stacked arrangement. 3. The transparent end housings are present on both sides in the expected positions. 4. The red wire connects the two sides correctly and follows the same overall routing as the normal 5-connector reference, with only slight curvature variation that is acceptable. 5. No missing parts, extra parts, swapped component types, misplacement, or physical damage are visible.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D9.json:1694:        "reasoning": "The reference images show a normal tray layout with two compartments: the left compartment contains three whole fruits stacked vertically, and the right compartment contains granola on the upper area with a mix of banana chips and nuts in the lower area. In the query image, the same overall configuration is present. The left compartment contains three fruits in the expected arrangement: two small citrus fruits and one larger red-yellow fruit, which is consistent with normal variation seen in the references. The right compartment also matches the expected composition: granola occupies the top/right section, while banana chips and nuts are grouped at the bottom. There is no missing item, no extra item, no obvious wrong component type, and no incorrect placement beyond normal variation. No physical damage is visible.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D9.json:3692:        "reasoning": "The reference images show the normal assembly pattern for this tray: the left compartment contains three fruits total, specifically two oranges/mandarins stacked above one apple/nectarine-like fruit. The right compartment contains granola on top and a nut/dried banana mix on the bottom. In the query image, the right compartment appears consistent with the references in both content and arrangement. However, the left compartment contains only two fruits: one orange and one apple/nectarine-like fruit. Compared with both normal references, one orange is missing from the left compartment. This is a logical anomaly due to wrong item count, not just positional variation.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D9.json:4075:          "evidence": "Both connectors are stacked close together in the center instead of being separated left and right with a visible blue wire connecting them across the image, as in all references.",
benchmark/results/v3_fixed/gpt_v9_sj3_k4_test_D5d.json:1533:            "variation": "The prominence and thickness of mucosal folds vary, from gentle broad undulations to more pronounced stacked folds.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D10.json:192:        "reasoning": "The retrieved reference images and the query all show the same PCB sensor module layout: 3-pin header on the left, central IC and blue trimmer, resistor stack on the right, and clear/black LED pair at the far right. The query matches the normal references closely in component presence, placement, orientation, and overall board shape. I do not see missing components, bent pins, cracked parts, contamination, or obvious surface damage. Minor differences are limited to slight pose/lighting variation, which are listed as normal false positives.",
benchmark/results/agent_v2/agent_test_D10.json:3402:        "evidence": "Localized irregular blob-like material is visible in the right-center/lower-right area next to the vertical resistor stack and above the lower black sensor, while the reference boards show this region as clean and well-defined.",
