-\subsection{Per-domain active self-evolution}
-\label{ssec:active_learning}
-
-Training-free agents cannot learn from their mistakes during
-inference.  A mild relaxation---letting the system query a handful of
-ground-truth labels \emph{once} per domain---should be attractive
-whenever a deployment has access to occasional human feedback. We test
-this under a simple protocol: on each CrossDomainVAD-11 domain $D$,
-(i) run v9 agent in passive mode on all test items, (ii) run v9 on
-the dev split, select the $K{=}10$ dev items the passive run was most
-uncertain about ($|s-0.5|$ smallest), (iii) query ground-truth labels
-only for those $10$ dev items from the dev manifest (test labels are
-never touched — this is semi-supervised domain adaptation, not active
-test-selection), (iv) embed the $10$ labelled neighbours with a
-DINOv2 CLS encoder and build a per-domain RAG index, (v) re-run v9 on
-test items with a compact ``domain prior'' derived from the top-$3$
-nearest DINOv2 neighbours injected into the turn-$1$ user message,
-and (vi) measure per-domain AUROC on the test items.
-
-\begin{table}[h]
-\centering
-\caption{\textbf{Active-learning pilot} (Qwen3.5-VL-27B, 4 pilot
-domains from the \texttt{manifests\_v2} taxonomy, $K{=}10$ oracle
-queries per domain from DEV, stratified $n{=}30$ test items per
-domain). Note the domain codes here follow \texttt{manifests\_v2}
-(where D5~$=$~MVTec-LOCO logical and D9~$=$~BraTS brain MRI),
-\emph{not} the D5~$=$~BraTS / D9~$=$~MVTec-LOCO naming of
-Table~\ref{tab:main_results}. We compare the \emph{passive} pass
-(v9 with no neighbours) to the \emph{active} pass (v9 with a
-compact DINOv2-retrieved neighbour prior).}
-\label{tab:active}
-\small
-\begin{tabular}{llccc}
-\toprule
-Code (v2) & Domain / source               & Passive AUROC & Active AUROC & $\Delta$ \\
-\midrule
-D1  & industrial / MVTec-AD              & $0.898$ & $0.971$ & $\mathbf{+7.33}$ \\
-D5  & MVTec-LOCO logical                 & $0.616$ & $0.576$ & $-4.00$ \\
-D9  & brain MRI / BraTS2021              & $0.602$ & $0.713$ & $\mathbf{+11.11}$ \\
-D12 & road safety / BDD100K              & $0.907$ & $0.902$ & $-0.44$ \\
-\midrule
-\multicolumn{2}{l}{\textbf{Mean} (4 domains)} & $0.756$ & $0.791$ & $\mathbf{+3.50}$ \\
-\bottomrule
-\end{tabular}
-\end{table}
-
-\paragraph{Finding 8: Active per-domain adaptation helps where the
-DINOv2 neighbour prior is informative.}  With $10$ labelled
-neighbours per domain the agent recovers $+7.3$ pp on industrial
-(D1, MVTec-AD) and $+11.1$ pp on brain MRI (D9, BraTS2021). On
-logical anomalies (D5, MVTec-LOCO) the active pass \emph{hurts}
-($-4.0$ pp), which is consistent with intuition: logical defects
-(wrong count, misordered components) are not well captured by a
-DINOv2-CLS visual-similarity retrieval. On road safety (D12) the
-passive baseline is already above $0.9$ and the neighbour prior
-does not add resolution ($-0.44$ pp).  The neighbour prior is
-injected as a compact summary sentence (``$N_\mathrm{anom}$ were
-anomalous, $N_\mathrm{norm}$ were normal''); we measured that
-injecting the full rationale texts instead caused the strict-JSON
-refutation schema to misfire on $\sim 85\%$ of items, whereas the
-summary form keeps parse-failure rate below $17\%$.  We position
-this as a concrete \emph{deployment} argument---not a training-free
-claim---and leave full scaling (all 12 domains, multiple $K$,
-multiple seeds, better retrieval than visual CLS for logical
-anomalies) as future work.
+% §4.7 "Per-domain active self-evolution" (DINOv2-CLS retrieval AL pilot)
+% removed 2026-04-20 in favour of the dedicated \S\ref{sec:verbalized}
+% Verbalized Self-Evolution chapter, which supersedes the retrieval pilot
+% with a natural-language rulebook construction (L1 + L2) over all 12
+% domains. The pilot's failure on D5 logical motivates the verbalized
+% approach (see \S\ref{sec:verbalized}'s motivation).
 
 \paragraph{Hyperparameter protocol and sensitivity.}
 All hyperparameters are frozen from the 20-item-per-domain calibration split and never re-tuned on dev/test: fusion weight $w{=}0.2$ (selected on GPT-5.4 calibration, re-used across backbones), sigmoid centre $m$ (global calibration expert median), online override $\rho>0.8$, descriptor-router rules (no metrics consulted), and calibration-router argmax. Leave-one-domain-out: the calibration-router--fusion gap is positive on 10/12 splits for SeedVL ($-0.8/+2.5/0.79$ pp min/max/std) and 9/12 for Qwen3.5; full table Appendix~\ref{app:loo}.

